  "body": "storage/state.py's _get_state_for_groups claims that if you pass in a `types` list with an entry with a state_key of None, the None will match all state_keys of the given type:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/106906a65e647d94a9d2faf1b3a626bc1f608a25/synapse/storage/state.py#L505-L509\r\n\r\nThis looks to be correct when we're querying the cache, thanks to:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/106906a65e647d94a9d2faf1b3a626bc1f608a25/synapse/storage/state.py#L461-L462\r\n\r\nHowever, it doesn't look like it's correct when we're querying the DB - where the None looks like it's turned into an `AND state_key = NULL` or similar?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/106906a65e647d94a9d2faf1b3a626bc1f608a25/synapse/storage/state.py#L239-L244\r\n",
